# Everything in this project is edited on Windows but RUN on the Paramshakti
# cluster (Linux). sbatch rejects a job script containing CRLF outright:
#
#   sbatch: error: Batch script contains DOS line breaks (\r\n)
#
# and bash silently mis-parses them elsewhere -- `export PARALLEL=1` in a CRLF
# file sets the variable to "1\r", which then fails every string comparison.
#
# So: force LF in the working tree for every file that a Linux tool reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
